From: PW3 Android port
Subject: [PW3] TextView: a text cursor that need not blink

A focused text field redraws its cursor every 500 ms for as long as it is
focused. On e-paper each redraw is a panel update: two a second while a field
waits for input (about 300 in one V36 session), and the stock reader's cursor
does not blink.

config_textCursorBlinks (default true, as before) set to false: the cursor is
drawn whenever it is shown at all, and nothing is posted to redraw it.

--- a/core/res/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/core/res/res/values/config.xml
@@ -3091,4 +3091,7 @@
          booted.  -->
     <integer name="config_stableDeviceDisplayWidth">-1</integer>
     <integer name="config_stableDeviceDisplayHeight">-1</integer>
+
